name=Requiem of the Dead: Odds and Ends
id=RFTDOddsAndEnds
modversion=1.1.0
require=RFTDCore
description=Odds and Ends - the family's catch-all for small self-contained modules, each with its own kill switch. RIPIT: Rip All on the right-click menu, working through the containers you have open. Sticky Headwear: your worn hat stays on when you take a hit. Quiet Horn: the vehicle horn still sounds, but it no longer draws zombies, so it cannot be used to herd a crowd off a street. Lumberjack: reversible weight scaling for logs, planks and other wooden items. Action Speed: per-family timed-action scaling (reading, foraging, cleaning, repair, dismantle, vehicle hood, vehicle mechanics, thread picking, ripping and cutting), moved here from Dragonfly because it is a world rule rather than an admin tool. Container Order: drag the container buttons in your own inventory sidebar into the order you want and have it stick, stored per character - moved here from Core so that a collection using Better Containers, Clean UI or any other container-reordering mod can switch it off. Inventory Collapse: Equipped and Hotbar buttons under your own inventory that fold those blocks out of the list, independently and remembered per character - moved here from Core alongside Container Order so a collection using Clean UI or another inventory UI mod can switch it off. Bookmark: an optional public-domain literature quote on login, purely for flavor - client-only and off by default; tick Welcome Message under Options, Mods to turn it on. Requires Requiem of the Dead: Core.
pzversion=42
